## Original Content
语义、关键词、全文和图谱检索各自覆盖不同问法。多路结果汇入候选池后再统一重排，可以把“有没有找到”和“应该排在哪里”分开检查，减少调参时的盲区。

## Summary
The article introduces ZGI, a hybrid retrieval method that combines semantic, keyword, full-text, and graph retrieval techniques. By gathering results from multiple sources into a candidate pool and applying unified reranking, it separates the processes of finding and ranking relevant information, reducing blind spots during parameter tuning.

## Key Points
- Multiple retrieval methods (semantic, keyword, full-text, graph) are used to cover different query aspects.
- Unified reranking is performed after collecting candidates from various retrieval paths.
- This approach decouples retrieval success from ranking order, allowing for separate evaluation.
- The method helps reduce blind spots in parameter tuning, improving retrieval efficiency.


